     ///     drive-letter order, so no rescan, start, commit, or batch is still running, then releases
     ///     every snapshot, retired and current, and finally gives the gates back. The gates are
     ///     released but never disposed: a caller admitted a moment after the disposed flag was set
     ///     waits for a gate, then throws <see cref="ObjectDisposedException" /> from its own
     ///     re-check, which is a caller's error to handle, while a disposed gate would throw from
     ///     that caller's release instead and hide the first exception. None of these gates ever
     ///     had its <see cref="SemaphoreSlim.AvailableWaitHandle" /> taken, so none holds anything
     ///     that needs a deterministic release.
